                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "edc38ff9-b449-483c-a7e2-faed96b7ccf5",
                                                "sense_id": "e047fe43-843f-3c6b-aeaa-e3d637342b60",
                                                "text": "In the area of the typography, or to be more precise the microtypography – the details of how the signs and spaces relate – there was a chance to create something new."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b833fe65-39c4-4030-8229-a48150cf3f24",
                                                "sense_id": "e047fe43-843f-3c6b-aeaa-e3d637342b60",
                                                "text": "If you're not sure of how to use these, leave them until you have time to experiment; as your work becomes more refined, you will need to know how these microtypography defaults should be adjusted too. Do not use forced bold, italic, outline, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0bbe8e51-c548-49bf-b12d-a9174e6febb0",
                                                "sense_id": "e047fe43-843f-3c6b-aeaa-e3d637342b60",
                                                "text": "Microtypography has to do with the details; setting the right glyph, getting the appropriate kerning and tracking, and making stylistic choices such as when to use small-caps. Micro techniques have received a lot of attention recently, […]"
                                            }
